'fr': in the FILE SECTION a VALUE clause belongs to a condition-name; COBOL 2002 allows it (X3.23-1985 VALUE rule 5.15.6(1))
VALUE spaces for the numeric item 'n1': a numeric item takes a numeric literal or ZERO (X3.23-1985 VALUE general rule 1a)
VALUE -1: the item 'n2' is unsigned (X3.23-1985 VALUE syntax rule 2)
VALUE 1.5 does not fit the PICTURE of the item 'n3' without losing nonzero digits (X3.23-1985 VALUE syntax rule 3)
VALUE literal (6 characters) is longer than the group 'g1' (2) (X3.23-1985 VALUE syntax rule 3)
'g2a' has a VALUE clause inside the group 'g2', which has one (X3.23-1985 VALUE rule 5.15.6(3))
'g3a' is not USAGE DISPLAY, inside the group 'g3' whose VALUE clause sets it as characters (X3.23-1985 VALUE rule 5.15.6(4))
'c1': VALUE ... THRU runs from the higher value to the lower (X3.23-1985 condition-name rule 2)
VALUE "x" for the numeric conditional variable 'c': a numeric item takes a numeric literal (X3.23-1985 VALUE general rule 1a)
VALUE 12 does not fit the PICTURE of the conditional variable 'c' without losing nonzero digits (X3.23-1985 VALUE syntax rule 3)
VALUE literal (2 characters) is longer than the conditional variable 'd' (1) (X3.23-1985 VALUE syntax rule 3)
